/*
 * Endpoint Name: LoginEndpoint
 * HTTP Method: POST
 * Backend Route: /api/auth/login
 * 
 * Future Request Contract: LoginRequest
 *   - Email: string (required, valid email)
 *   - Password: string (required, min 6 chars)
 * 
 * Future Response Contract: LoginResponse
 *   - Token: string (JWT token)
 *   - User: UserDto (user profile without PasswordHash)
 * 
 * Required Permission: None (public endpoint)
 * 
 * Related Domain Entities:
 *   - User (Domain/Entities/User.cs)
 * 
 * Validation Steps:
 *   1. Validate Email format
 *   2. Validate Password not empty
 *   3. Check Email exists in database
 *   4. Verify password hash matches
 * 
 * Implementation Steps:
 *   1. Receive LoginRequest
 *   2. Query User by Email from AppDbContext
 *   3. Verify PasswordHash using BCrypt.Verify()
 *   4. Generate JWT token with user claims (UserId, Email)
 *   5. Map User entity to UserDto (exclude PasswordHash)
 *   6. Return LoginResponse with token and user info
 * 
 * Error Cases:
 *   - 400 Bad Request: validation errors (invalid email format, empty password)
 *   - 401 Unauthorized: invalid credentials (email not found or password mismatch)
 *   - 500 Internal Server Error: unexpected database or hashing errors
 * 
 * EXPLICIT NOTE: NOT IMPLEMENTED IN PHASE 3C
 * This file is a TODO skeleton only. Real implementation will be done in later phase.
 */

